Coverage absence verified: `ls app/*_test.odin harness/*_test.odin` → "No such file or directory"; `grep -rn "qos_mode_manual|qos_apply_auto|qos_revert" app/*_test.odin core/*_test.odin` → no matches; `grep -rn "draw_hud|draw_qos_panel|App\b" harness/*.odin` → no matches (harness/main.odin imports only `pp "../core"`). The E2E tier authors the outcome directly, not the app logic: demos/qos_auto.dem ends `at 3000ms lane 1 streaming express` / `at 3000ms lane 1 email best_effort` / `at 3000ms weights 1 50 30 20` — the weights command is harness-authored; demos/qos_manual.dem has no `lane` directive after `weights 1 60 25 15`, so no manual-then-assign or revert scenario is captured anywhere.

